Reject invalid day-of-year values before indexing month_days.

When strptime() parses "%j" without a year, glibc_fix() fills in the
current year and walks month_days to derive the month and day. In a
non-leap year, day 366 advances the month index to 12 and then reads
month_days[12], beyond its 12 elements. Reject out-of-range yday values
before the walk.

A smaller reproducer is:
    Rscript --vanilla -e 'strptime("366", "%j", tz="UTC")'

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1a.R), not
carried here.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 4687865079201792 (libFuzzer_r_datetime,
Global-buffer-overflow READ 4).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #384, filed 2026-10-16.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

--- a/src/main/datetime.c
+++ b/src/main/datetime.c
@@ -927,6 +927,10 @@ static void glibc_fix(stm *tm, bool *invalid)
     if(tm->tm_yday != NA_INTEGER) {
 	// since we have yday, let that take precedence over mon/mday
 	int yday = tm->tm_yday, mon = 0;
+	if (yday < 0 || yday >= days_in_year(1900 + tm->tm_year)) {
+	    *invalid = true;
+	    return;
+	}
 	while(yday >= (tmp = days_in_month(mon, tm->tm_year))) {
 	    yday -= tmp;
 	    mon++;
